// src/user/ime/session_kind.pdx -- G11-M1-001 (paideia-os #2314)
//
// KIND_IME_SESSION = 0x1D4, derived over KIND_WINDOW (0x1C1).
// LINEAR cap: no R_MINT bit; each session is a fresh mint by the
// future KIND_IME_ROUTER (G11-M1-003, paideia-os #2316) and is
// consumed on focus loss (session close via revoke, or terminal
// commit-and-close by the toolkit binding).
//
// Design authority: design/compositor/pwp-spec-vocabulary.md §2.18
// (KIND_IME_SESSION). Sibling landings in this same G11.M1 wave:
// §2.19 KIND_IME_PROVIDER (#2315) and §2.20 KIND_IME_ROUTER (#2316)
// are the future companions and are OUT OF SCOPE for this row --
// this file defines the LINEAR session cap only.
//
// SPEC RESHAPING NOTE. §2.18 pins the parent kind as
// KIND_IPC_ENDPOINT (= 5) at the top-of-graph level; this landing
// reshapes the immediate parent to KIND_WINDOW (0x1C1) per the
// row prompt for G11-M1-001. The rationale is that an IME session
// is anchored to a specific window's text field (window_kind_id
// + field_id) at mint time, not to a bare IPC endpoint -- the
// endpoint framing was the top-level catalogue shape, whereas the
// substrate that mints has to name the focus surface directly.
// KIND_WINDOW does NOT hold R_MINT on KIND_IME_SESSION (the LINEAR
// discipline forbids it); the mint gate is held by the future
// KIND_IME_ROUTER, and the parent slot recorded here is the
// derivation-graph parent (kind_id resolution + revoke chain), not
// the mint authority. When KIND_IME_ROUTER lands at #2316 its
// KIND_ID becomes the mint authority the substrate consults.
//
// PITFALL P10 MITIGATION. Pitfall register row P10 (dual-IME race,
// Wayland `text-input-v3`) is closed by two invariants: LINEARITY
// (one open session per surface per moment; a second mint against
// the same (window, field) evicts and revokes the first) and
// EXCLUSIVE ROUTING through KIND_IME_ROUTER (§2.20; #2316). This
// file establishes the first invariant. The second is landed by
// the router file; the pair together closes P10.
//
// PARENT WINDOW REFERENCE. KIND_WINDOW landed at src/user/compositor/
// window_kind.pdx (G7-M3-001, paideia-os #2254) at ordinal 0x1C1.
// This file references that ordinal by numeric literal to sidestep
// a module-order dependency in the encoder's linker step; the
// coordination point is the derived-kinds registry, which lists
// every ordinal atomically at batch close.
//
// SLOT ALLOCATION. 0x1D4 is verified free by grep over
// src/kernel/core/cap/*.pdx and src/user/**/*.pdx as of this
// landing (adjacent occupants: 0x1D0 RESERVATION_HOLDER_KIND,
// 0x1D1 RP_COMPOSITOR_KIND_FORWARD; 0x1D2..0x1D3 free but reserved
// by adjacent recovery-plane landings; 0x1D5..0x1DF free). Main
// should advance the "Next free derived-kind tag" line in
// design/architecture/next-wave-derived-kinds.md past 0x1D4 at
// batch close.
//
// LINEARITY DISCIPLINE (P10 mitigation).
//
//   * NO R_MINT bit is declared on this kind. A KIND_IME_SESSION
//     is minted BY the KIND_IME_ROUTER authority (that router
//     holds R_MINT on this derived family) and never by a client.
//     Once minted, the cap is held by exactly one client at
//     exactly one moment; the compositor's cap-table dispatch
//     enforces the no-clone contract at the kernel boundary
//     (single-owner slot).
//
//   * Consume-on-close contract: the REVOKE op atomically stamps
//     the `revoked` bit in the row header, deducts the row from
//     the pool (row goes back to the free list), and returns
//     the cap slot. ONE REVOKE PER MINT. A second revoke attempt
//     against an already-revoked row returns IME_SESSION_ALREADY_REVOKED;
//     a preedit / commit op against an already-revoked row returns
//     IME_SESSION_STALE. The row is not reusable -- a fresh session
//     requires a fresh mint by the router against a fresh focus event.
//
//   * The three mutating rights (SET_PREEDIT, CLEAR_PREEDIT,
//     COMMIT_TEXT) mutate row fields IN PLACE; they do NOT clone
//     the cap and they do NOT consume it. Only REVOKE consumes.
//     COMMIT_TEXT is a separate wire operation from SET_PREEDIT --
//     the novel-clean split (this file's design bias) is that a
//     commit is NOT a "final preedit set followed by close": it
//     is a distinct wire event that bumps commit_seq and clears
//     the preedit, leaving the session open for the next
//     composition round. Session close is the LINEAR revoke, and
//     it is orthogonal to whether the last preedit was committed
//     or cleared.
//
//   * The compositor is the ONLY authority allowed to observe or
//     revoke a KIND_IME_SESSION row on the client's behalf:
//     R_IME_SESSION_OBSERVE is compositor-held (debug printer);
//     R_IME_SESSION_REVOKE is held by both the client (voluntary
//     close) and the router (focus-loss eviction). A client that
//     leaks its cap by process death is cleaned up by the
//     compositor-side revoke path (a cap held by a dead client is
//     recovered when its cap table is torn down; the row's
//     revoked bit is stamped and the row goes back to the free
//     list).
//
// PREEDIT + COMMIT AS DISTINCT WIRE OPS (novel-clean).
//
// The Wayland `text-input-v3` protocol conflates preedit updates
// and commits into a single "done" event, which is one of the
// pitfalls the P10 mitigation exists to close. This landing pins
// them as SEPARATE ops:
//
//   * SET_PREEDIT publishes an uncommitted candidate string with a
//     cursor position. The client (application-side toolkit) can
//     render this in-line as ghost text; the compositor knows the
//     text is provisional and is not part of the field's value.
//
//   * COMMIT_TEXT atomically finalizes a string into the field
//     (independent of whatever the current preedit says), bumps
//     the commit_seq (a monotone counter the toolkit uses to
//     detect duplicates and out-of-order events), and CLEARS the
//     preedit as a side effect. A composition round is a sequence
//     of SET_PREEDIT ops terminated by exactly one COMMIT_TEXT (or
//     one CLEAR_PREEDIT for a cancel).
//
//   * CLEAR_PREEDIT cancels the current provisional candidate
//     without committing anything and without bumping commit_seq.
//
// The session STAYS OPEN across composition rounds; only REVOKE
// closes it. This is the "one session per focus" contract:
// focus-gain mints, focus-loss revokes, any number of composition
// rounds happen in between.
//
// FINGERPRINT. One legacy-suffixed mint fingerprint per the
// standard klog convention (matches surface_commit / window_kind /
// kind_tui_canvas precedent). Emitted once on successful mint by
// the future substrate; no fingerprint on the preedit / commit /
// clear / revoke paths.
//
// LABEL PREFIX: `ime_session_` throughout, sidestepping paideia-as
// reserved-word collisions (`loop`, `if`, `let`, `write`, ...).
//
// MECE SCOPE. Single file under src/user/ime/. No mod.pdx exists
// in this directory yet; the registry marker
// `; wave0-b8-04: session_kind` marks this module's slot if main
// decides to add one. This landing touches no other file.
//
// FAILURE TAXONOMY BAND. 0xFFFFEB70..0xFFFFEB7F, freshly allocated.
// Verified free by grep over src/**/*.pdx and tests/**/*.pdx as
// of this landing (adjacent occupied bands: KIND_TUI_CANVAS
// 0xFFFFEB10..1F, KIND_TLS_TRUST 0xFFFFEB20..27, KIND_NIC
// 0xFFFFEB28..2F, KIND_SCHEMA_REGISTRY 0xFFFFEB30..3F,
// KIND_SCHEMA_HANDLE shares 0xFFFFEB35..39). 0xFFFFEB70..0xFFFFEB7F
// is the next free 16-slot page past those.
//
// =============================================================================

module SessionKind = structure {

  // ==========================================================================
  // SECTION 1.1 -- KIND ORDINAL + PARENT
  // ==========================================================================

  pub let KIND_IME_SESSION      : u64 = 0x1D4
  pub let KIND_IME_SESSION_BASE : u64 = 0x1C1   // = KIND_WINDOW (G7-M3-001)

  // ==========================================================================
  // SECTION 1.2 -- RIGHTS
  // ==========================================================================
  //
  // Bit assignments follow the surface_commit / kind_tui_canvas /
  // tonemap_kind style (a sparse map so the dispatcher can
  // `test rax, R_*` and branch on the single bit). CRITICALLY:
  // there is NO R_MINT bit. A LINEAR cap does not carry mint
  // rights; the mint authority (KIND_IME_ROUTER, #2316) is the
  // sole minter.
  //
  //   R_COMMIT_TEXT     -- atomically finalize a string into the field;
  //                        bumps commit_seq; clears preedit as side effect
  //   R_QUERY_STATE     -- read commit_seq, preedit, cursor (no mutation)
  //   R_SET_PREEDIT     -- publish an uncommitted candidate string
  //   R_CLEAR_PREEDIT   -- cancel the current provisional candidate
  //   R_REVOKE          -- LINEAR consume: end the session (focus loss,
  //                        client-side voluntary close, or router
  //                        eviction on second mint against same field)
  //   R_IME_OBSERVE     -- compositor-held debug printer (§2.20 router
  //                        also holds this)
  //
  // R_IME_SESSION_ALL is the OR of every declared bit and is the
  // exact right-set the KIND_IME_ROUTER mint gate stamps at
  // derivation time. The client typically holds R_IME_SESSION_CLIENT
  // (everything except R_IME_OBSERVE, which stays with the
  // compositor). R_REVOKE stays with the client because voluntary
  // close IS the client-side session-done gesture.

  pub let R_IME_SESSION_COMMIT_TEXT   : u64 = 0x01
  pub let R_IME_SESSION_QUERY_STATE   : u64 = 0x02
  pub let R_IME_SESSION_SET_PREEDIT   : u64 = 0x04
  pub let R_IME_SESSION_CLEAR_PREEDIT : u64 = 0x08
  pub let R_IME_SESSION_REVOKE        : u64 = 0x10
  pub let R_IME_SESSION_OBSERVE       : u64 = 0x20    // R_IME_OBSERVE
  pub let R_IME_SESSION_ALL           : u64 = 0x3F

  // The client-visible right-set at mint time: everything except
  // R_IME_OBSERVE (which stays with the compositor authority for
  // the debug printer path).
  pub let R_IME_SESSION_CLIENT        : u64 = 0x1F

  // ==========================================================================
  // SECTION 1.3 -- ROW LAYOUT (ImeSessionFields, 64 bytes)
  // ==========================================================================
  //
  // One cache line per row (surface_commit / kind_tui_canvas /
  // tonemap_kind precedent). Every mutating op edits one packed
  // field IN PLACE. The row is written by exactly one client at a
  // time (LINEAR discipline); no cache-coherence fencing beyond
  // the atomic header stamp REVOKE performs, because the mutation
  // ops and the revoke op are serialized by the client's own
  // control flow.
  //
  // Row layout (offsets in bytes):
  //
  //   [+0]  header:
  //             in_use[63:56]        1 iff row is allocated
  //             revoked[55:55]       1 iff REVOKE has run (linear-consume gate)
  //             reserved[54:0]       0 at mint; future flags land here
  //
  //   [+8]  window_pack: parent-field identity
  //             window_kind_id[63:32]  the target window's KIND_WINDOW
  //                                    cap_table slot; never rebound
  //             field_id[31:0]         which text field within the window
  //                                    (0 if the window has only one
  //                                    focusable text field; otherwise
  //                                    a toolkit-assigned id)
  //
  //   [+16] provider_kind_id: u64
  //             low 32 bits: the KIND_IME_PROVIDER (§2.19, #2315)
  //             cap_table slot servicing this session. MUST be nonzero
  //             at mint time (the router selects a provider before
  //             minting the session cap). High 32 bits reserved.
  //
  //   [+24] preedit_pack: current preedit (uncommitted candidate)
  //             preedit_text_offset[63:32]  interned-string offset into
  //                                         the compositor-side preedit
  //                                         string pool (0 = empty
  //                                         preedit; the string pool
  //                                         reserves offset 0 as the
  //                                         empty-string sentinel)
  //             preedit_cursor[31:0]        cursor position within the
  //                                         preedit string (0 = at
  //                                         start; must be <= preedit
  //                                         string length)
  //
  //   [+32] commit_seq: u64
  //             monotone counter, incremented by COMMIT_TEXT. 0 at mint;
  //             each COMMIT_TEXT bumps by 1 and returns the new value.
  //             The toolkit uses this to detect duplicate commits and
  //             to order commits against provisional preedit state
  //             (a preedit_pack observed with commit_seq == N pins
  //             the preedit as "current as of commit N").
  //
  //   [+40..63] reserved for future extension (locale hint, IME state
  //             flags, script-shaping mode). Zero at mint.
  //
  // The "atomic-batch" shape of surface_commit is DELIBERATELY NOT
  // present here: an IME session is not a transaction, it is a
  // long-lived interaction endpoint. Each of SET_PREEDIT /
  // COMMIT_TEXT / CLEAR_PREEDIT publishes a distinct state change
  // that the compositor forwards to the router without buffering.

  pub let IME_SESSION_ROW_BYTES : u64 = 64
  pub let IME_SESSION_MAX       : u64 = 16    // pool ceiling (compositor
                                              // may have several open
                                              // sessions across multiple
                                              // focused surfaces on
                                              // different workspaces)

  // Offsets into the 64-byte row.
  pub let IME_SESSION_OFF_HEADER        : u64 = 0
  pub let IME_SESSION_OFF_WINDOW_PACK   : u64 = 8
  pub let IME_SESSION_OFF_PROVIDER      : u64 = 16
  pub let IME_SESSION_OFF_PREEDIT_PACK  : u64 = 24
  pub let IME_SESSION_OFF_COMMIT_SEQ    : u64 = 32
  pub let IME_SESSION_OFF_RESERVED      : u64 = 40

  // Header bit positions (in the top byte of the [+0] word).
  //   in_use   = bit 56 of the header word
  //   revoked  = bit 55 of the header word
  pub let IME_SESSION_HDR_IN_USE_BIT   : u64 = 56
  pub let IME_SESSION_HDR_REVOKED_BIT  : u64 = 55

  // Empty-preedit sentinel: preedit_text_offset == 0 means "no
  // provisional candidate currently pending". The compositor-side
  // preedit string pool MUST reserve offset 0 for the empty string
  // (this constraint is inherited by the future pool landing).
  pub let IME_SESSION_PREEDIT_EMPTY     : u64 = 0

  // Provider must be nonzero at mint time (router pre-selects).
  pub let IME_SESSION_PROVIDER_NONE     : u64 = 0

  // ==========================================================================
  // SECTION 1.4 -- OPS
  // ==========================================================================
  //
  // Every op is arity ONE (row_id in target_ptr, sub-op in
  // op_arg[7:0]; the mutating ops carry additional payload in
  // op_arg[63:8]). Dispatch lands in a future kernel-side
  // cap_handler_ime_session milestone (G11-M2-001, TBD when the
  // router lands its mint gate). The REVOKE op is the LINEAR
  // consume: its handler MUST test-and-set the revoked bit
  // atomically and MUST move the row to the free list before
  // returning.
  //
  //   SET_PREEDIT      payload: preedit_text_offset | preedit_cursor
  //                    (packed as preedit_pack: offset[63:32] | cursor[31:0])
  //   COMMIT_TEXT      payload: text_offset (interned string to commit).
  //                    Handler bumps commit_seq, clears preedit,
  //                    returns the new commit_seq in rax.
  //   CLEAR_PREEDIT    payload: none; clears preedit_pack.
  //   QUERY_STATE      payload: field_id (0=commit_seq, 1=preedit_pack,
  //                    2=window_pack, 3=provider_kind_id)
  //   REVOKE           payload: none; consumes the cap (LINEAR).
  //   DEBUG_PRINT      payload: none; R_IME_OBSERVE required.

  pub let IME_SESSION_OP_SET_PREEDIT    : u64 = 0
  pub let IME_SESSION_OP_COMMIT_TEXT    : u64 = 1
  pub let IME_SESSION_OP_CLEAR_PREEDIT  : u64 = 2
  pub let IME_SESSION_OP_QUERY_STATE    : u64 = 3
  pub let IME_SESSION_OP_REVOKE         : u64 = 4
  pub let IME_SESSION_OP_DEBUG_PRINT    : u64 = 5
  pub let IME_SESSION_OP_MAX            : u64 = 5

  // Field IDs for the QUERY_STATE op.
  pub let IME_SESSION_FIELD_COMMIT_SEQ  : u64 = 0
  pub let IME_SESSION_FIELD_PREEDIT     : u64 = 1
  pub let IME_SESSION_FIELD_WINDOW      : u64 = 2
  pub let IME_SESSION_FIELD_PROVIDER    : u64 = 3
  pub let IME_SESSION_FIELD_MAX         : u64 = 3

  // ==========================================================================
  // SECTION 1.5 -- FAILURE TAXONOMY (0xFFFFEB70..0xFFFFEB7F)
  // ==========================================================================
  //
  // A fresh 16-wide band, disjoint from every documented kind band.
  // Verified free by grep over src/**/*.pdx + tests/**/*.pdx as of
  // this landing (see file header for adjacency).

  pub let IME_SESSION_OK                  : u64 = 0
  pub let IME_SESSION_TAIL_ENOSPC         : u64 = 0xFFFFEB7F
  pub let IME_SESSION_TAIL_BAD_ARG        : u64 = 0xFFFFEB7E
  pub let IME_SESSION_MINT_BAD_PARENT     : u64 = 0xFFFFEB7D  // parent kind != KIND_WINDOW
  pub let IME_SESSION_MINT_BAD_WINDOW     : u64 = 0xFFFFEB7C  // window_kind_id == 0
  pub let IME_SESSION_MINT_BAD_PROVIDER   : u64 = 0xFFFFEB7B  // provider == 0
  pub let IME_SESSION_MINT_BAD_RIGHTS     : u64 = 0xFFFFEB7A
  pub let IME_SESSION_MINT_DUPLICATE      : u64 = 0xFFFFEB79  // second mint against
                                                              // same (window, field);
                                                              // caller must first
                                                              // revoke the prior one
  pub let IME_SESSION_BAD_SLOT            : u64 = 0xFFFFEB78
  pub let IME_SESSION_WRONG_KIND          : u64 = 0xFFFFEB77
  pub let IME_SESSION_BAD_RIGHTS          : u64 = 0xFFFFEB76
  pub let IME_SESSION_BAD_PREEDIT_OFFSET  : u64 = 0xFFFFEB75  // preedit offset OOB
  pub let IME_SESSION_BAD_PREEDIT_CURSOR  : u64 = 0xFFFFEB74  // cursor > preedit len
  pub let IME_SESSION_BAD_COMMIT_OFFSET   : u64 = 0xFFFFEB73  // commit offset OOB
  pub let IME_SESSION_ALREADY_REVOKED     : u64 = 0xFFFFEB72  // LINEAR consume violation
  pub let IME_SESSION_STALE               : u64 = 0xFFFFEB71  // op after revoke
  pub let IME_SESSION_REVOKE_ALREADY      : u64 = 0xFFFFEB70
  pub let IME_SESSION_DECODE_BAD          : u64 = 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF

  // ==========================================================================
  // SECTION 1.6 -- STATS COUNTER SLOTS
  // ==========================================================================
  //
  // The kernel-side substrate will publish an _ime_session_stats
  // [u64; 8] table; slot indices are named here so cross-module
  // bumpers agree. REVOKES vs MINTS lets a boot-log observer verify
  // the LINEAR invariant (MINTS >= REVOKES; deficit == in-flight
  // sessions + client-death recoveries).

  pub let IME_SESSION_ST_MINTS       : u64 = 0
  pub let IME_SESSION_ST_REVOKES     : u64 = 1
  pub let IME_SESSION_ST_COMMITS     : u64 = 2
  pub let IME_SESSION_ST_PREEDITS    : u64 = 3
  pub let IME_SESSION_ST_CLEARS      : u64 = 4
  pub let IME_SESSION_ST_QUERIES     : u64 = 5
  pub let IME_SESSION_ST_REFUSED     : u64 = 6
  pub let IME_SESSION_ST_DOUBLE_REV  : u64 = 7   // ALREADY_REVOKED occurrences
  pub let IME_SESSION_ST_MAX         : u64 = 8

  // ==========================================================================
  // SECTION 1.7 -- FINGERPRINT (one line, legacy-suffixed)
  // ==========================================================================
  //
  // pdx_kind_ime_session_meta: emitted once on successful mint by
  // the future substrate. The legacy-suffix convention is what
  // tools/verify-fingerprint-coverage.sh enumerates, so this
  // literal is the machine-checkable name of the milestone. No
  // fingerprint on the preedit / commit / clear / revoke paths.
  //
  // Size = 50 bytes (49 chars + trailing NUL), per the +1 rule.
  pub let pdx_kind_ime_session_meta : [u8; 50] = "ime session mint ok [legacy: IME SESSION MINT OK]\0"

  // Short field-name string constant for future debug-print use
  // (mirrors surface_commit_k_commit_id / tmk_k_lut_id precedent).
  pub let ime_session_k_commit_seq  : [u8; 11] = "commit_seq\0"

  // ==========================================================================
  // SECTION 2 -- PACKERS + VALIDATORS (schema-only, pure leaves)
  // ==========================================================================
  //
  // Every function in this section is a pure, unsafe-bodied leaf
  // with small immediates (no MOVABS r64, imm64 anywhere), returns
  // its result in rax, and clobbers only rax + one scratch
  // register. Encoder-conservative pattern per surface_commit /
  // kind_tls_trust / tonemap_kind (no `and r11, imm64`, no
  // two-operand `imul` with immediate).

  // ime_session_op_valid(op) -> 1 iff op in [0, OP_MAX=5].
  pub let ime_session_op_valid : (u64) -> u64 !{} @{} =
    fn (op: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "G11-M1-001 (paideia-os #2314): dispatch op validator. Admits 0..5 (SET_PREEDIT..DEBUG_PRINT). Small immediate. Labels prefixed ime_session_ov_.",
      block: {
        cmp rdi, 5;
        ja  ime_session_ov_no;
        mov rax, 1;
        ret;
      ime_session_ov_no:
        xor rax, rax;
        ret
      }
    }

  // ime_session_field_valid(f) -> 1 iff f in [0, FIELD_MAX=3].
  pub let ime_session_field_valid : (u64) -> u64 !{} @{} =
    fn (f: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "G11-M1-001 (paideia-os #2314): QUERY_STATE field-id validator. Admits 0..3 (commit_seq, preedit, window, provider). Labels prefixed ime_session_fv_.",
      block: {
        cmp rdi, 3;
        ja  ime_session_fv_no;
        mov rax, 1;
        ret;
      ime_session_fv_no:
        xor rax, rax;
        ret
      }
    }

  // ime_session_window_pack(window_kind_id, field_id)
  //   -> window_kind_id[63:32] | field_id[31:0].
  // Both halves masked to 32 bits so an out-of-range argument
  // cannot smear into a neighbor field. Row-write helper for
  // window_pack at [+8].
  pub let ime_session_window_pack : (u64, u64) -> u64 !{} @{} =
    fn (window_kind_id: u64) (field_id: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "G11-M1-001 (paideia-os #2314): pack window_kind_id[63:32] | field_id[31:0] per row layout at [+8]. Encoder-conservative build of the 32-bit mask via shl+shr to avoid MOVABS r64, 0xFFFFFFFF. Straight-line, no labels needed.",
      block: {
        // rax = field_id & 0xFFFFFFFF (via shl 32 / shr 32)
        mov rax, rsi;
        shl rax, 32;
        shr rax, 32;

        // r10 = window_kind_id shifted left 32 (natural mask + placement)
        mov r10, rdi;
        shl r10, 32;

        or  rax, r10;
        ret
      }
    }

  // ime_session_preedit_pack(text_offset, cursor)
  //   -> text_offset[63:32] | cursor[31:0].
  // Mirror of window_pack. Row-write helper for preedit_pack at [+24].
  pub let ime_session_preedit_pack : (u64, u64) -> u64 !{} @{} =
    fn (text_offset: u64) (cursor: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "G11-M1-001 (paideia-os #2314): pack text_offset[63:32] | cursor[31:0] per row layout at [+24]. Encoder-conservative build of 32-bit mask via shl+shr. Straight-line.",
      block: {
        mov rax, rsi;
        shl rax, 32;
        shr rax, 32;

        mov r10, rdi;
        shl r10, 32;

        or  rax, r10;
        ret
      }
    }

  // ime_session_hdr_pack() -> canonical row header at mint time.
  // Only the substrate's tail_alloc sets in_use (bit 56); revoked
  // (bit 55) stays 0 until REVOKE fires. Mirror of tui_hdr_pack /
  // surface_commit_hdr_pack.
  pub let ime_session_hdr_pack : () -> u64 !{} @{} =
    fn () -> unsafe {
      effects: {}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "G11-M1-001 (paideia-os #2314): canonical row header at mint time. Only in_use written by tail_alloc; revoked stays 0 until REVOKE fires. Mirror of surface_commit_hdr_pack. Straight-line.",
      block: {
        xor rax, rax;
        ret
      }
    }

  // ime_session_provider_valid(provider_kind_id) -> 1 iff nonzero.
  // The router pre-selects a provider before minting; a zero
  // provider is caught at mint time as IME_SESSION_MINT_BAD_PROVIDER.
  pub let ime_session_provider_valid : (u64) -> u64 !{} @{} =
    fn (provider_kind_id: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "G11-M1-001 (paideia-os #2314): provider-slot nonzero validator. IME_SESSION_PROVIDER_NONE (0) is the invalid sentinel. Labels prefixed ime_session_pv_.",
      block: {
        cmp rdi, 0;
        je   ime_session_pv_no;
        mov  rax, 1;
        ret;
      ime_session_pv_no:
        xor  rax, rax;
        ret
      }
    }

  // ==========================================================================
  // SECTION 3 -- MINT / OP STUBS (schema-only; real handlers land later)
  // ==========================================================================
  //
  // The real cap_handler_ime_session lives in a future kernel-side
  // milestone that follows the KIND_IME_ROUTER landing (#2316).
  // That handler MUST:
  //
  //   MINT: validate window != 0, provider != 0, no prior session
  //         against (window, field); tail_alloc a row; write header
  //         (in_use=1, revoked=0), window_pack, provider_kind_id,
  //         preedit_pack=0, commit_seq=0; bump ST_MINTS; emit the
  //         pdx_kind_ime_session_meta fingerprint exactly once.
  //
  //   SET_PREEDIT: check revoked==0; write preedit_pack; bump
  //                ST_PREEDITS.
  //
  //   COMMIT_TEXT: check revoked==0; atomically increment commit_seq;
  //                clear preedit_pack; return the new commit_seq in
  //                rax; bump ST_COMMITS.
  //
  //   CLEAR_PREEDIT: check revoked==0; clear preedit_pack (no
  //                  commit_seq change); bump ST_CLEARS.
  //
  //   REVOKE: cmpxchg the revoked bit from 0 to 1 in the header word;
  //           on cmpxchg failure return IME_SESSION_ALREADY_REVOKED;
  //           return the row to the free list (in_use cleared); bump
  //           ST_REVOKES.
  //
  // Until that handler lands, every dispatch of a mutating op
  // returns IME_SESSION_STALE from the stubs below so downstream
  // harnesses observe a well-formed refusal rather than a fabricated
  // success.

  // ime_session_mint(window, field, provider) -> IME_SESSION_STALE.
  // Signature-authoritative: window_kind_id in rdi, field_id in rsi,
  // provider_kind_id in rdx. The future handler consumes exactly
  // these three arguments in this order.
  pub let ime_session_mint : (u64, u64, u64) -> u64 !{} @{} =
    fn (window: u64) (field: u64) (provider: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "G11-M1-001 (paideia-os #2314): LINEAR mint stub. Returns IME_SESSION_STALE (0xFFFFEB71) until the kernel-side cap_handler_ime_session lands. A fabricated mint would defeat the LINEAR invariant this file exists to establish. Small immediate (fits imm32, sign-extends). Straight-line.",
      block: {
        mov rax, 0xFFFFEB71;
        ret
      }
    }

  // ime_session_set_preedit(row_id, text_offset, cursor) -> IME_SESSION_STALE.
  pub let ime_session_set_preedit : (u64, u64, u64) -> u64 !{} @{} =
    fn (row_id: u64) (text_offset: u64) (cursor: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "G11-M1-001 (paideia-os #2314): SET_PREEDIT stub. Returns IME_SESSION_STALE until the kernel-side handler lands. Small immediate. Straight-line.",
      block: {
        mov rax, 0xFFFFEB71;
        ret
      }
    }

  // ime_session_commit_text(row_id, text_offset) -> IME_SESSION_STALE.
  // The real handler returns the new commit_seq (u64) on success;
  // the stub returns the STALE sentinel so a caller cannot mistake
  // the return for a valid seq.
  pub let ime_session_commit_text : (u64, u64) -> u64 !{} @{} =
    fn (row_id: u64) (text_offset: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "G11-M1-001 (paideia-os #2314): COMMIT_TEXT stub. Real handler returns the post-increment commit_seq; stub returns IME_SESSION_STALE so downstream code cannot mistake the return for a valid seq. Small immediate. Straight-line.",
      block: {
        mov rax, 0xFFFFEB71;
        ret
      }
    }

  // ime_session_clear_preedit(row_id) -> IME_SESSION_STALE.
  pub let ime_session_clear_preedit : (u64) -> u64 !{} @{} =
    fn (row_id: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "G11-M1-001 (paideia-os #2314): CLEAR_PREEDIT stub. Returns IME_SESSION_STALE until the kernel-side handler lands. Small immediate. Straight-line.",
      block: {
        mov rax, 0xFFFFEB71;
        ret
      }
    }

  // ime_session_revoke(row_id) -> IME_SESSION_STALE.
  // The real handler does the linear-consume cmpxchg; the stub does
  // NOT stamp the revoked bit -- a fabricated revoke would defeat
  // the LINEAR invariant this file establishes.
  pub let ime_session_revoke : (u64) -> u64 !{} @{} =
    fn (row_id: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "G11-M1-001 (paideia-os #2314): REVOKE stub. Real handler does the cmpxchg linear-consume; stub returns IME_SESSION_STALE without stamping the revoked bit (a fabricated revoke would defeat the LINEAR invariant). Small immediate. Straight-line.",
      block: {
        mov rax, 0xFFFFEB71;
        ret
      }
    }
}
